#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:435
msgid ":fa:`box-archive` Intersphinx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:439
msgid ":bash:`.github/scripts/inventories.py`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:440
msgid ":bash:`docs/src/_inventory` :fa:`folder`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:443
msgid ""
"Cross-references into the documentation of another project are resolved by "
"`intersphinx`_, which downloads an inventory of targets from each project in"
" the ``INTERSPHINX_URLS`` mapping of :bash:`docs/src/conf.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:447
msgid ""
"Since ``geovista`` builds its documentation in ``nitpicky`` mode with "
"``--fail-on-warning``, every one of those projects would otherwise be a hard"
" build dependency: a site that is briefly unavailable fails the build, both "
"for the inventory it could not download *and* for each cross-reference that "
"inventory would have resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:453
msgid ""
"To avoid this, a copy of each inventory is **vendored** in the "
":bash:`docs/src/_inventory` directory and offered to `intersphinx`_ as a "
"fallback location. A build always prefers the remote inventory, so it "
"carries the current targets; the vendored copy is consulted only when the "
"remote cannot be reached, and ``sphinx`` does not warn when a later location"
" succeeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:462
msgid ""
"Adding a project to ``INTERSPHINX_URLS`` **must** be accompanied by its "
"vendored inventory. Refresh them with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:469
msgid ""
"Then commit whichever :bash:`*.inv` files have changed. The :bash:`ci-"
"inventories.yml` workflow runs the same task monthly and raises a pull-"
"request when an inventory has moved on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:473
msgid ""
"Should every location for an inventory fail, say for a project added without"
" a vendored fallback, the :bash:`intersphinx_resilience` extension disables "
"``nitpicky`` mode for the remainder of the build, reporting the failure "
"without failing on it. The documentation is then built, but unresolved "
"cross-references go unreported, so treat a degraded build as a warning to "
"refresh the inventories rather than a pass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:485
msgid ":fa:`comments` Tooltips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:489
msgid ":bash:`docs/src/_static/js` :fa:`folder`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:491
msgid ":bash:`tests/docs/test_tooltips.py`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:493
msgid ""
"A `sphinx-tippy`_ tooltip previews the target of a link without following "
"it. Which links are given one is settled twice over, by two ``conf.py`` "
"settings that behave quite differently:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:497
msgid "Tooltip Skip Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:502
msgid "Setting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:504
msgid "``tippy_skip_urls``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:504
msgid ""
"Regular expressions matched against the ``href`` of a link as the tooltip is"
" **generated**. A link skipped here has no tooltip in the payload of the "
"page at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:508
msgid "``tippy_skip_anchor_classes``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:508
msgid ""
"Class names consulted in the browser as the tooltip is **attached**. A link "
"skipped here still has a tooltip generated for it, and merely never has one "
"shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:516
msgid ""
"A ``tippy_skip_urls`` pattern is applied with :python:`re.match` against the"
" ``href`` exactly as it was written into the page, which is bare between "
"sibling pages (``clouds.html``) and directory-prefixed from anywhere else "
"(``../generated/gallery/domain/clouds.html``). A pattern for one shape "
"silently misses the other, so :bash:`conf.py` generates both, anchored at "
"the end so that a deliberate ``tippy-gv-`` fragment may still opt its target"
" back in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:527
msgid ""
"``tippy_skip_anchor_classes`` **replaces** the extension defaults of "
"``headerlink`` and ``sd-stretched-link`` rather than extending them, so both"
" must be restated alongside any addition. Dropping ``sd-stretched-link`` is "
"what allows a ``sphinx-design`` card to raise a tooltip carrying the heading"
" and opening paragraph of the page that it links to, since such a card is an"
" anchor stretched over the whole card body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:534
msgid ""
"Tooltips are skipped for the `sphinx-gallery`_ thumbnails, which render a "
"tooltip of their own that a second one would collide with, and for the "
"`sphinx-tags`_ badges, whose tooltip repeats the text of the badge that "
"raised it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:539
msgid ""
"The ``tippy.js`` and ``popper`` runtime bundles are **vendored** in the "
":bash:`docs/src/_static/js` directory, since the extension otherwise loads "
"them from a third-party ``CDN`` on every page, leaving a reader with no "
"tooltips at all when that host cannot be reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:547
msgid ""
"The :bash:`tests/docs/test_tooltips.py` unit tests hold all of the above in "
"place, inspecting the built payload of each page for the static behaviour "
"and driving a browser for the rest. See :ref:`tippy-gv-developer-testing-"
"browser-tests` for further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:557
msgid ":fa:`plug` Sphinx Directives"
msgstr ""

