#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:571
msgid ":fa:`toggle-off` :bash:`readingtime`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:573
msgid "Usage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:579
msgid ""
"Calculates an *estimated* reading time of an entire page based on the number"
" of words and a default *words-per-minute* reading heuristic for technical "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:583
msgid ""
"The words are counted on the *parsed* page rather than in its source, so "
"directive names, option lines, link targets, comments and substitution "
"definitions do not inflate the estimate, and a body generated by another "
"directive is included in it. A substitution is counted where it expands, "
"once per use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:589
msgid ""
"The default rate is ``150`` words-per-minute. :cite:t:`brysbaert-2019` puts "
"most adults between ``175`` and ``300`` words-per-minute on English non-"
"fiction, averaging ``238``; these pages are pitched below that band because "
"they alternate prose with code and output that a reader works through line "
"by line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:595
msgid ""
"Accepts an optional ``<duration>`` reading time (in minutes), a literal "
"reading time to be quoted rather than calculated. Reach for it on a page "
"whose estimate is wrong for a reason the word count cannot see, such as a "
"tutorial whose reader stops to run every snippet. On a page the count gets "
"right it is a figure that has to be revised by hand every time the page "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:601
msgid ""
"The directive then creates a branded :bash:`readingtime` banner in-situ "
"e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:607
msgid "Generates the banner:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:611
msgid ""
"Alternatively, provide an optional *words-per-minute* to override the "
"directive default when calculating the reading time estimation e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:618
msgid ""
"Generates the following banner, using ``1,000`` words-per-minute to "
"calculate the estimate to read this :ref:`tippy-gv-developer-documentation` "
"page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:626
msgid ""
"A default *words-per-minute* value will always be used to generate a reading"
" time for a directive with no arguments i.e., ``.. readingtime::``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:632
msgid ""
"Any other argument fails the build. Quietly falling back on the default "
"would publish an estimate the author never asked for, and nothing would say "
"that the argument had been misspelled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:636
msgid ""
"Every page a reader reads start to finish opens with a banner, placed at "
"column zero after the title and before the first section heading. A page "
"carries exactly one. The two live examples above sit well below the first "
"heading of this page, which is what makes them demonstrations and not "
"banners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:641
msgid ""
"A page that is **navigated** rather than read carries none: the site root "
"and the section landing pages, the reference pages whose body a directive "
"generates, the release notes, the lookup tables (:ref:`tippy-gv-reference-"
"glossary`, :ref:`tippy-gv-reference-bindings`, :ref:`tippy-gv-reference-"
"environment` and :ref:`tippy-gv-reference-about`), and :ref:`tippy-gv-"
"developer-towncrier`, whose body is an include of a page that carries the "
"banner already. Putting a duration on a glossary invites a reader to treat "
"it as a chapter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:653
msgid ""
"Those pages are named in ``EXEMPT`` in "
":bash:`tests/docs/test_readingtime_coverage.py`, each with the reason beside"
" it, and the gate there holds every other page to the rule. It derives the "
"pages it governs from :bash:`docs/src` rather than listing them, so a new "
"page is covered from the day it lands. Adding one means adding the banner or"
" adding the reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:665
msgid ":fa:`palette` Theme"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:671
msgid ":bash:`tests/docs` :fa:`folder`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:673
msgid ""
"The documentation is rendered with `sphinx-book-theme`_, which is layered "
"upon `pydata-sphinx-theme`_. Note that ``sphinx-book-theme`` pins ``pydata-"
"sphinx-theme`` to an **exact** version, so the pair of them only ever move "
"together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:680
msgid ""
":bash:`docs/src/_static/sidebar_toggle.js` is a **workaround**, not a "
"feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:682
msgid ""
"``sphinx-book-theme`` renders a second primary and secondary sidebar toggle "
"and hides the ``pydata-sphinx-theme`` pair, yet both themes bind their "
"handlers to the **first** match i.e., the hidden one. That leaves the "
"visible buttons inert and both sidebars unreachable on a narrow viewport. "
"The shim forwards clicks to the bound button of each pair, and self-retires "
"once only one button remains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:688
msgid ""
"It also closes the primary dialog at :python:`(min-width: 992px)`, since the"
" dialog inherits the classes of the sidebar, and therefore its wide-viewport"
" collapsed state, which would otherwise strand the dialog open but invisible"
" over a page that it blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:693
msgid ""
"The two halves retire on different schedules, so **re-check both on every "
"theme bump**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/documentation.rst:696
msgid ""
"The theme chrome is assembled in the browser and so is beyond the reach of "
"the :ref:`tippy-gv-developer-testing-image-tests`, which compare ``pyvista``"
" scenes rather than page furniture. It is instead covered by the "
":ref:`tippy-gv-developer-testing-browser-tests`, which exercise both "
"sidebars either side of the ``992`` pixel theme breakpoint, and across a "
"resize through it."
msgstr ""

